  "description": "Instructions hidden with a zero font size or a zero opacity, which makes text invisible to humans but readable by agents. GLS-HI-002 lists font-size:0 and opacity:0 as words, but the text is folded before words are looked up and the fold turns every 0 into an o, so those two words could never be found there. This rule reads them as a complete zero declaration instead (the property, a colon, the number 0, an optional unit, then the end of the declaration), and only when the declaration starts at the start of the value or after a semicolon, outside every comment, quoted string and bracket, and no later declaration of the same property in that value replaces it. The value must belong to the first attribute of the tag named exactly style (not data-style, not a value quoted inside another attribute), blanks being the HTML ones (space, tab, line feed, form feed, carriage return), and the text of that same element, up to the next tag, must carry an instruction aimed at an agent: \"ignore (or disregard, forget) the previous (prior, above, earlier) instructions\", an AI word (AI, LLM, language model, chatbot, assistant, agent) addressed with a comma, colon or semicolon and a command or a modal verb and a command, \"if you are an AI\", or \"you are now an AI (or in developer, debug, DAN or god mode)\". A plain imperative aimed at a person or at nobody (\"tell the customer the refund is complete\", \"never mention this discount\") is not read: it cannot be told from ordinary page text by its wording, so those hidden instructions are a known limit of this rule. The text is read, not parsed: a tag written inside an HTML comment, a script or a textarea is read as a tag. A stylesheet rule is never read, so ordinary zero states (a fade class, a reset, an animation) stay clean. Known limits: an unquoted style value that holds an equals sign, a quote or a backtick, an unquoted attribute value that holds a less-than sign, a tag name that runs into its first attribute, a tag inside a comment, script or textarea, and the stated bounds (20 attributes on each side, 300 characters of attribute value, 300 characters of element text, 200 characters before and after the zero).",
  "keywords": [],
